id: quiz.k8s.incident
kind: quiz
track: kubernetes
title: First five minutes of an incident
question: Users report 500s from a Kubernetes service. What do you do first?
expects:
  - scope
  - events
  - endpoints
  - logs previous
  - rollback
misuse:
  - restart everything => destroys evidence and may widen the outage
  - assume networking => skipping the workload layer wastes the first minutes
related:
  - k8s.debugging-workflow
  - k8s.events
  - k8s.endpoints
  - k8s.rollback
  - recipe.incident-diagnosis
follow_ups:
  - how would you find the cause if the pods were already replaced?
answer: |
  Scope it (which routes, which replicas, since when), then read state before
  acting: replicas desired vs ready, events sorted by time, container state, and
  whether the Service has endpoints. Only then choose rollback or fix-forward.
